\b\fs56 FINAL RECOMMENDATION — THE BEST FOR AURA.RADIO (EXPANDED MEDIA AI PLATFORM)\b0\fs28

This is the single, unified, production-ready stack for building a complete AI-powered media system covering:

* Radio
* Podcasts
* Video
* Live streaming sessions

\b CORE PRINCIPLE\b0
One pipeline. Multiple media inputs. Clean architecture.

\b 1. MEDIA INGESTION LAYER (NEW — UNIFIED INPUT)\b0
Handles all content types:

* Live radio streams (RTMP/WebRTC)
* Podcast uploads (MP3/WAV)
* Video files (MP4/MKV)
* Live sessions (real-time streams)

All inputs are normalized before processing.

\b 2. AUDIO EXTRACTION (FOR VIDEO)\b0

* Extract audio from video automatically
* Standardize format (WAV, 16kHz)

This ensures every media type feeds the same AI engine.

\b 3. SPEECH-TO-TEXT (CORE ENGINE)\b0
Primary Model:

* OpenAI Whisper large-v3

Why:

* Industry-leading accuracy
* Handles noisy broadcast environments
* Multilingual support
* Proven production reliability

This remains the foundation of the system.

\b 4. SPEAKER DIARIZATION (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\b0
Model:

* pyannote speaker-diarization 3.1

Why:

* Separates speakers (host, guest, callers)
* Handles overlapping speech
* Broadcast-grade output

Required for professional-level output.

\b 5. VIDEO INTELLIGENCE LAYER (NEW)\b0

* Frame sampling every few seconds
* Scene/context detection
* Timeline synchronization with transcript

This upgrades the system from audio-only to full media intelligence.

\b 6. REAL-TIME PROCESSING (LIVE CAPTIONS)\b0

* WebSocket-based streaming
* Chunked audio processing
* Instant caption delivery

Supports:

* Live radio
* Live podcasts
* Live video sessions

\b 7. AI ENHANCEMENT LAYER\b0

* Automatic summaries
* Topic extraction
* Semantic search indexing
* Real-time insights

Transforms raw transcripts into usable intelligence.

\b 8. STORAGE + SEARCH\b0

* Store transcripts, speakers, and metadata
* Index for fast querying
* Enable “search inside audio/video”

\b 9. DEPLOYMENT STRATEGY\b0
Hybrid (CPU + GPU):

* CPU for baseline operation
* GPU for scaling and performance

Cost-efficient and future-proof.

\b FINAL PIPELINE\b0

Media Input (Audio / Video / Stream)
->
Ingestion Layer
->
Audio Extraction (if video)
->
Whisper large-v3 (Transcription)
->
Pyannote 3.1 (Speaker Diarization)
->
Video Intelligence (Scene Analysis)
->
AI Layer (Summaries, Topics, Search)
->
WebSocket Output (Live Captions)
->
Storage + Archive

\b WHAT THIS SYSTEM DELIVERS\b0

* Real-time captions for all media
* Speaker-aware transcripts
* Video + audio intelligence
* Searchable media archives
* Scalable AI processing engine

\b WHAT IS INTENTIONALLY EXCLUDED\b0

* Experimental streaming ASR (unstable)
* Over-engineered pipelines
* Unnecessary external dependencies
* Voice cloning by default (legal risk)

\b BOTTOM LINE\b0
This is no longer just a radio system.

It is a complete:
AI-Powered Media Intelligence Platform

Capable of handling:

* Radio broadcasts
* Podcasts
* Video content
* Live interactive sessions

All within a single, unified architecture.

This foundation is production-ready, scalable, and aligned with long-term system growth.
